 "prompt": "the page isnt loading and server runs on 3000 but db is hosted on 5000",
 "output" : "Root cause: Not a port/CORS/DB config issue — both servers were already running correctly (frontend :3000, backend :5000). The Lifts page was stuck because its API call to GET /api/lifts hit a 404: the route existed in liftRoutes.js but was never mounted in server.js — the mount line was commented out and pointed at a non-existent filename (liftsRoutes instead of liftRoutes).

Fix applied:


app.use('/api/lifts', require('./routes/lifts/liftRoutes'));
Nodemon auto-restarted the backend on save, and GET /api/lifts now returns 200 {"success":true,"data":[]} instead of 404.
Reload the page in your browser — the Lifts view should now load. If any other newer pages (inspections/defects/rectifications) are also blank, they're in the same state — routes exist under backend/src/routes/ but are still commented out in server.js, same root cause.",
