"prompt": "can u add a csv only import feature",
"output": "Backend — new POST /api/lifts/import endpoint (liftController.js, wired in liftRoutes.js). It takes { rows: [...] }, creates each row individually (not insertMany) so one bad row doesn't sink the batch, and returns { created, failed: [{ row, liftCode, message }] } — verified live with a duplicate-code and missing-field row, both correctly rejected with per-row reasons while the valid row succeeded.

Frontend — in the Lifts page (Lifts.jsx):

Import CSV button next to Export, gated behind canEdit like Add/Edit/Delete already are.
The file picker is restricted to .csv — and even if a browser allows picking something else, Lifts.jsx explicitly rejects any filename not ending in .csv with an error toast before it ever reaches the parser. That's the "CSV only" part.
utils/csvImport.js: a small hand-rolled CSV parser (handles quoted/escaped fields) plus a header-alias map so both machine (liftCode) and human (Lift Code) column names are recognized.
A "Download the CSV template" link under the page title, so users know the expected columns without guessing.
An Import Results dialog reporting how many rows succeeded and listing exactly which rows failed and why."
